  {
    "episode_id": 48329,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48329.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "I was playing football and I thank God for football because literally it kept me focused enough to get my act together. And in this country, if you will work hard, If you dream big, the most amazing things can happen. And my mother never gave up on me. She told me I was blessed with the greatest citizenship in the world being an American. And she told me that with God as my foundation, if I would not quit on myself. If I would do the work, she was not going to do it for me. If I would do the work, all things are possible. And one of the things that you read in my book is now if you do the work, this country will afford you the best future you could dream of. And we should be proud of America. We should stand up and shout from the mountain tops that we are blessed beyond recognition because we are Americans. And we do get a second chance at life. We do have a story of redemption. Our country has had it. And I've been blessed to live.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_05",
